+## Module lists and blocklists
+
+The *topaz* device (codename *tapas*) requires a set of kernel module list
+files that specifies which vendor modules should be loaded at boot and
+which should be blocked.  These files are dropped from the `topnotchfreaks`
+`kernel_msm-5.15` `zepharo` branch and are now part of the Apex
+repository under `kernel/`:
+* `modules.list.msm.topaz` – list of modules to load.
+* `modules.systemdlkm_blocklist.msm.topaz` – system DLKM blocklist.
+* `modules.vendor_blocklist.msm.topaz` – vendor DLKM blocklist.
+
+They are automatically copied into the kernel tree by the helper script
+`topaz-module-lists.sh` that is invoked from `apply.sh`.
+
+**Conflict notes** – None of the modules blocked by `modules.vendor_blocklist.msm.topaz`
+interfere with the apex pentest autoloading logic.  No conflicts were
+observed during the build.
